# DigiSwasthya Product Definition Document (PDD)

# Part 8 — User Journeys

---

# Purpose

This section defines every meaningful user journey in DigiSwasthya.

A user journey is an end-to-end business path a user follows to achieve one outcome.

Journeys do not describe screens or technical implementation.

They describe:

- Who performs the journey
- Preconditions
- Step sequence
- Entities affected
- Outcomes
- Failure exits

Every journey must move well-defined entities through well-defined states and capabilities.

If a journey exists in the product but not in this document, the product definition is incomplete.

---

# Journey Structure

Every journey uses this structure:

```
Journey Name
Actor
Goal
Preconditions
Steps
Entities Affected
Success Outcome
Failure / Exit Paths
Notes
```

For brevity in large lists, short-form journeys use:

```
Journey | Actor | Preconditions | Steps | Success | Failures
```

