# H. Fulfilment & Delivery

---

## H1. Allocate Inventory to Order

- Actor: Stockist
- Preconditions: Order Accepted
- Steps: Allocate batches/qty → Reservations updated
- Failures: Insufficient sellable stock; expired batch selected

## H2. Pack Order

- Steps: Confirm packed contents → Order = Packed

## H3. Generate Dispatch

- Steps: Create Delivery from packed order → Assign if needed → Ready to dispatch

## H4. Assign Delivery Staff

- Steps: Choose delivery boy/staff → Delivery = Assigned

## H5. Mark Out for Delivery

- Steps: Start route → Delivery = Out for Delivery → Order may become Dispatched

## H6. Complete Full Delivery

- Steps: Mark delivered → Capture proof/recipient if required → Delivery = Delivered → Order = Delivered
- Pharmacy may confirm receipts

## H7. Partial Delivery

- Steps: Deliver available items → Record delivered vs pending → Order = Partially Delivered
- Remaining items follow continuation or cancellation rules

## H8. Failed Delivery

- Steps: Mark failed with reason → Delivery = Failed → Goods handling path (retry / return to stockist)

## H9. Retry Failed Delivery

- Steps: Reassign/reschedule → Out for Delivery again

## H10. Pharmacy Records Received Quantities

- Actor: Pharmacy
- Steps: Open delivery/order → Enter received qty → Report shortage/damage if any

## H11. Report Shortage on Receipt

- Steps: Record short qty → Notify stockist → May create adjustment/return path

## H12. Report Damaged Products on Receipt

- Steps: Record damage → Attach evidence optional → Initiate return/adjustment path

## H13. Manage Delivery Routes

- Actor: Stockist
