# R. Recovery & Exception Journeys

---

## R1. Order Cancelled After Invoice Issued

- Controlled exception: Cancel/void path restricted; may require credit note or admin policy rather than silent cancel

## R2. Payment Approved Against Already Paid Invoice

- Control: Block over-allocation or route to overpayment handling rule

## R3. Return Raised After Eligibility Expiry

- Failure: Request blocked with reason

## R4. Credit Exceeds Invoice Outstanding

- Steps: Apply up to outstanding → Remaining credit stays available

## R5. Inventory Goes Insufficient After Accept

- Steps: Stockist cannot pack full qty → Partial fulfilment / cancel remainder / reject continuation

## R6. Batch Expires After Allocation Before Dispatch

- Steps: Block dispatch of expired batch → Reallocate or adjust order

## R7. Duplicate GST on Registration

- Failure: Registration/verification blocked or flagged for admin

## R8. Connection Removed With Open Orders

- Steps: New orders blocked → Open orders continue or freeze per rules → Settlement/returns still processable under policy

## R9. Invoice Before Dispatch Attempt

- Policy journey: Allowed only if business rules explicitly permit bill-ahead; otherwise blocked

## R10. Offline Continuation / Retry After Failure

- Actor: Any
- Steps: Action fails due to connectivity → User retries → No duplicate side effects if already succeeded
- Notes: Detailed NFR/error behaviour later

